---
title: Quickstart
summary: A static page with one interactive island, from empty route to working demo, in five minutes.
related:
  - start/install
  - regions/client-islands
---

This walks the shortest path to something real: a page that ships as pure HTML with a single island that hydrates. If you have not added the package yet, do [Install](/docs/start/install) first.

## 1. Turn the page into a Page

Opt the route out of the Kit client so it ships no framework JS.

```ts
// src/routes/+layout.ts
export const csr = false;
```

## 2. Write a normal Svelte component

Nothing ogygia-specific here — it is just a component.

```svelte
<!-- src/lib/Counter.svelte -->
<script>
  let { start = 0 } = $props();
  let count = $state(start);
</script>

<button onclick={() => (count += 1)}>count is {count}</button>
```

## 3. Mark the import to make it an island

The import attribute is the whole opt-in. The rest of the page stays static HTML.

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+page.svelte -->
<script>
  import Counter from '$lib/Counter.svelte' with { wake: 'load' };
</script>

<h1>A static page</h1>
<p>This heading and text ship zero JS.</p>

<Counter start={3} />
```

That is a working islands page. The heading and paragraph are server HTML forever; only `Counter` downloads JS, and only because you marked it.

## 4. See it live

The counter below is a real island on this very page, hydrated on `load` exactly like the code above:

<script>
  import LoadLive from '$lib/demos/LoadLive.svelte' with { wake: 'load' };
</script>

<div class="doc-demo-row">
  <div class="doc-demo"><LoadLive /></div>
</div>

<style>
  .doc-demo-row { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .doc-demo {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-md, 12px);
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    max-width: 22rem;
  }
</style>

## 5. Change when it wakes

Swap the strategy and the island hydrates later — no other change:

```svelte
import Counter from '$lib/Counter.svelte' with { wake: 'idle' };     // when the browser is idle
import Counter from '$lib/Counter.svelte' with { wake: 'visible' };  // when scrolled into view
import Counter from '$lib/Counter.svelte' with { wake: '(max-width: 600px)' }; // on small screens
```

